tp://openlibrary.org/books/OL37824059M/The_boy_who_harnessed_the_wind","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/boywhoharnessedw0000kamk_j3c2","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12724890-S.jpg","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publish_date":"2015","copyright_date":"2015","publish_country":"nyu","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL6787654A","name":"William Kamkwamba"}],"oclc_numbers":["1267537541"],"dewey_decimal_class":["[E]"],"edition_name":"Young readers edition.","description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"When 14-year-old William Kamkwamba's Malawi village was hit by a drought in 2001, everyone's crops began to fail. His family didn't have enough money for food, let alone school, so William spent his days in the library. He came across a book on windmills and figured out how to build a windmill that could bring electricity to his village. Everyone thought he was crazy but William persevered and managed to create a functioning windmill out of junkyard scraps. Several years later he figured out how to use the windmill for irrigation purposes\"--"},"contributions":["Mealer, Bryan, author","Hymas, Anna, illustrator"],"subject_people":["William Kamkwamba (1987-)"],"subject_places":["Malawi"],"subjects":["Juvenile literature","Mechanical engineers","Biography","Windmills","Electric power production","Irrigation"],"title":"The boy who harnessed the wind","by_statement":"William Kamkwamba and Bryan Mealer ; illustrated by Anna Hymas","publishers":["Scholastic Inc."],"publish_places":["New York, NY"],"isbn_13":["9780545946032"],"isbn_10":["0545946034"],"pagination":"301 pages","number_of_pages":301,"ocaid":"boywhoharnessedw0000kamk_j3c2","source_records":["ia:boywhoharnessedw0000kamk_j3c2","amazon:0545946034","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17"],"full_title":"The boy who harnessed the wind","covers":[12724890],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL15190422W"}],"key":"/books/OL37824059M","local